  "notes": "PR is an abbreviation of English \"Public Relations,\" but in Japanese it is used more broadly than in English to mean any kind of promotion or self-promotion.\n\nSENSE 1 — PROMOTION/PUBLICITY:\n- PR{活動|かつどう}: PR/promotional activities\n- PRする: to promote, to publicize\n- PR{動画|どうが}/PRビデオ: promotional video\n- PR{戦略|せんりゃく}: PR strategy\n\nSENSE 2 — SELF-PROMOTION:\nExtremely common in Japanese job hunting ({就職|しゅうしょく}{活動|かつどう}).\n- {自己|じこ}PR: self-promotion statement (a standard part of Japanese job applications)\n- PRポイント: selling points, strengths to highlight\n- {自分|じぶん}をPRする: to promote/sell oneself\n\nUSAGE:\nIn Japanese, PR has a broader, more casual meaning than English \"public relations.\" It often simply means \"to promote\" or \"to appeal,\" without the formal corporate communications connotation.",
